  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Rhode Island received $825M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The federal government awarded 4,475 contracts in the state, with an average award size of $184K. Obligations fell 8.8% year over year. The Department of Defense obligated $673M, making the Department of Defense the largest buying agency in the state for the fiscal year to date. Engineering Services is the largest industry by obligations at $299M. SEACORP, LLC is the largest vendor by obligations at $113M. Historical annual obligations show variation: FY21 totaled $928M, FY22 totaled $1.2B, FY23 totaled $1B, FY24 totaled $1.2B, FY25 totaled $906M, and FY26 totaled $825M. The top agencies after the Department of Defense are the Department of Veterans Affairs at $54.5M and the General Services Administration at $37.6M. The top industries after Engineering Services are Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $108M and Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing at $71.4M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 8.8% year over year. Annual totals show a peak of $1.2B in FY22 and FY24, then a decline to $906M in FY25 and $825M in FY26. Rhode Island obligations have moved between $928M and $1.2B across the last six fiscal years. The current-year total is partial because figures are fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal contracting in Rhode Island?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer with $673M in obligations. The Department of Veterans Affairs and the General Services Administration follow with $54.5M and $37.6M respectively. SEACORP, LLC, RAYTHEON COMPANY, and RITE-SOLUTIONS, INC. are the top three vendors with $113M, $87M, and $67.5M respectively. Engineering Services, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences, and Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing are the largest industries by obligations at $299M, $108M, and $71.4M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
